        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="1347" n="1189" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1189"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Norwegian Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In view of your very kind expressions in
                    regard to the matter during the interview I had the pleasure to have with you, I
                    have the honor to advise you that the President, as evidence of his good will
                    toward the Government and people of Norway, has appointed Mr. Charles H. Graves,
                    of Minnesota, ambassador extraordinary of the United States of America on
                    special mission, to represent this Government at the ceremonies attending the
                    coronation of His Majesty Haakon VII, King of Norway.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
